{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone","id":1114281,"title":"Inspiration needed: Circle of the Crone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T14:38:11-07:00","id":1114281,"title":"Inspiration needed: Circle of the Crone","content":"Hey guys and girls. I need some help.<br /> I'm building my city and in turn the covenants within the city. Each clan and covenant has some area of influence (within the mortal society) in which they are dominant: Law Enforcement, Media, The Criminal Underworld etc. And I'm having some trouble figuring out what my Circle of the Crone's influence would/should be. So I'm hoping someone here is able to help me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Context: New Orleans 2015. The Circle consists of a single coven and is fighting a losing battle against the Lancea et Sanctum. They have suffered an agonizing defeat and as a result they've lost one of their two domain, which means that they are now held up in the Warehouse District of New Orleans.<br /> <br /> So my question to you is: If this was your campaign, what sphere of mortal influence would your battered (and nearly broken) Circle of the Crone fight to maintain control of above all else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:57:54-07:00","id":1114291,"title":"","content":"One thing that i did with the Circle of the Crone is that they had influence within the mortals gangs. Essentially, each cult or coven would sponsor a mortal gang and then they would pit the gangs against one another. The coven with the strongest gang would be the strongest coven. There would be varying rules to determine the extent that the vampires are allowed to meddle. Generally indirect influence was accepted but ghouling everyone (or other such ideas) wasnt. That would encourage each coven to treat their gang as a pet project to grow within adversity.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T15:14:52-07:00","id":1114295,"title":"","content":"Hm, my Circle of the Crone covens typically have a hand in the more natural stuff; like conservation movements, local botanists, florists, and stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T15:18:01-07:00","id":1114296,"title":"","content":"&quot;Concepts: Riot grrl, working-class matriarch, indigenous people\u2019s rights campaigner, reclusive wealthy occultist, dissolute swinger, technopagan clubber, body modification enthusiast, voodoo priest, strange-eyed street ganger, witchy librarian, aging old-school libertine; suspiciously friendly laird of the manor.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Circle seems to have a lot of influence in occult circles, native populations, and &quot;pagan&quot; occult circles. Lots of repressed groups plus magic people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:12:17-07:00","id":1114307,"title":"","content":"Entertainment might be one. Entertainers are modern day idols and bards, and a natural gift being used in the modern age likely appeals to them. As an addition, it gives them influence and money. That seems like more of a Ventrue Crone way to do things, however.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could have cults, strippers, prostitutes, hunters and trappers, internet circles, and at the risk of stereotyping the area, good old fashioned human magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:16:35-07:00","id":1114308,"title":"","content":"There are some intereseting answers here. Thanks guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> On top of your suggestions I'm considering them preying on those whose lives are in shambles: Influencing the homeless or local rehab centers and support groups. People who need something or someone new to believe in and help them get back on their feet.<br /> What doe you guys think of those ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:19:45-07:00","id":1114309,"title":"","content":"Mortal vodoun practitioners is the no brainer answer. If you insert a few of them as old money or local influential businesses involved in tourism and/or alcohol who believe they owe their success to a handful of traditional vodoun practices that have been tainted by Cruac, it gives the Acolytes a foothold in local politics due to their influence over the city economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:30:34-07:00","id":1114310,"title":"","content":"The docks. You already have them in a werehouse so just go from there.<br /> Edit: I don't know if New Orleans has a dockside worth controlling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 07-10-2017, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:45:18-07:00","id":1114459,"title":"","content":"This won't help you much in New Orleans game but my Circle of the Crone has a lot of pull in local hard right neo pagan movements. So I guess gangs would be the answer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T01:53:32-07:00","id":1114480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone?p=1114310#post1114310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I don't know if New Orleans has a dockside worth controlling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the key freight hubs for the US. If the Circle can't do anything with that, then they're not trying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T03:04:15-07:00","id":1114495,"title":"","content":"Good to know, I realised after I first posted that as we were talking about a real city it could be land locked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:35:08-07:00","id":1114540,"title":"","content":"Despite the name, the Warehouse District is not littered with warehouses. It's a buffer zone between the Central Business District and the French Quarter (which makes it prime real estate for dabbling in traditional finance oriented businesses, or more vampire centric activities like elysiums and feeding grounds) And the shipping terminals technically arent in its jurisiction where offical human borders are concerned. They are in the Riverfront, although most (but not all) shipping terminals are to the immediate east of the Warehouse district.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T09:55:31-07:00","id":1114646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone?p=1114495#post1114495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to know, I realised after I first posted that as we were talking about a real city it could be land locked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite the opposite, New Orleans is barely land to begin with. Its built on a swamp filled river delta. The Mississippi River, some large lakes and the Gulf of Mexico meet there in a mash of brackish water. A lot of the city is even under sea level with dykes holding back the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:44:02-07:00","id":1114709,"title":"","content":"The first thing that come to my mind is drug trafficking and nightclub business, just think of anything or anywhere that bring humans back to a more primitive state (from mindless dancing to tripping on acid)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T12:47:04-07:00","id":1114710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone?p=1114296#post1114296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Concepts: Riot grrl, working-class matriarch, indigenous people\u2019s rights campaigner, reclusive wealthy occultist, dissolute swinger, technopagan clubber, body modification enthusiast, voodoo priest, strange-eyed street ganger, witchy librarian, aging old-school libertine; suspiciously friendly laird of the manor.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Circle seems to have a lot of influence in occult circles, native populations, and &quot;pagan&quot; occult circles. Lots of repressed groups plus magic people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's perfect for New Orleans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:28:10-07:00","id":1114781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone?p=1114459#post1114459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This won't help you much in New Orleans game but my Circle of the Crone has a lot of pull in local hard right neo pagan movements. So I guess gangs would be the answer</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of place is your game in set then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T00:32:55-07:00","id":1114967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114281-inspiration-needed-circle-of-the-crone?p=1114781#post1114781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of place is your game in set then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Middle-eastern Poland. Theory behind it is that number of local CoC vampires that are now aniclla were members of various local fascist movements before the WWII. Those groups also had a tendency to incorporate some pagan symbols and rhetoric(same as in other European countries at that time). Now since this movements(or rather their modern reiterations) are again active it seemed only natural that they would be within CoC sphere of influence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T02:43:06-07:00","id":1115439,"title":"","content":"<br /> The parks and swamps. <a href=\"https://www.nola.gov/parks-and-parkways/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nola.gov/parks-and-parkways/</a> (Is there a way to make links here? Who knows. Google the new orleans parks and/or swamps) <br /> <br /> The lone-man rangers, rapists, druggies, hippies, millenials, fisherman, and voodoo practictioners who love them. The night-patrolling policeman in the park. The crocodiles!! The lonely dark boardwalks through the swamp.. For a group making their last stand, claiming these areas would be a bit like guerilla warfare. Come, try and find us! But it would also have some bold advantages (like the &quot;neutral areas&quot; considered critical for all the freakin' parades and the golf course) It would have history in the various small parks. It would be scattered throughout the city, and so hard to attack directly and concertedly. <br /> <br /> Symbolically: The wild places, both in terms of &quot;nature&quot; and perhaps in terms of &quot;godliness&quot;. The natural world isn't the sole domain of the crone, but they probably would have a stronger affinity. And it would be neat to be a mortal walking a fine line between a world of the &quot;wild swamp vampires&quot; and the &quot;upstanding religious vampires&quot;. (An idea, though I have no idea how you play your groups..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:49:57-07:00","id":1116097,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, if they are beleaguered and barely holding it together, how about echoing that thematically with their areas of influence?<br /> <br /> You could give them a focus on hospitals, nursing homes, ambulance companies, maybe first responders, like emts, fire-fighters and cops. These are parts of the mortal world set up to deal with it when people are just barely holding on by a thread. Maybe even have them down to exactly one public hospital, which is constantly threatened with closure.<br /> <br /> Concepts:<br /> <br /> Third shift icu nurse who has seen it all, but still stands in religious awe of the mutilation some people survive.<br /> <br /> Ambulance driver who drives a little slower for the ones with bad karma, if you get my drift.<br /> <br /> Cop who mostly works the ER, recording evidence in GSWs and administering rape kits.<br /> <br /> Patient in an Alzheimer's Care Facility with a very active... social life.<br /> <br /> Psychiatrist who decides if hospitalized patients are ready to be released based on if they have suffered enough. And will have someone committed for the right bribe.<br /> <br /> Nursing home orderly who decides when the elderly deserve a painless way out.<br /> <br /> Doctor who works at a free clinic for sex workers.<br /> <br /> Home Health Aide who works overnight shifts, lives in the projects, but is a high ranking Spiritualist Preacher.<br /> <br /> Former firefighter who was horribly burned on the job because he absolutely refused to leave the scene before the rest of his company.<br /> <br /> Morgue Tech who really, really enjoys his work.<br /> <br /> Biowaste disposal company owner that can make anything disappear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}